          <mxGeometry x="64" y="1320" width="2752" height="37" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="explain-1" value="This panel isolates the reference-guided training path: x_ref → B → E → S_ref → G(S_ref,y′) → D/R/W+B → losses. There is NO random-style input in this path. The same shared G/D/P also train on random x_rand and reconstruction x_rec, shown in (b)/(c)/(d); the equations below describe that full objective." vertex="1" parent="notes" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=0;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=18;fontStyle=0;fontColor=#202020;">
          <mxGeometry x="64" y="1367" width="2752" height="37" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="explain-2" value="L&lt;sub&gt;D&lt;/sub&gt; = E[(1 − D(x))₊] + (1/3) ∑&lt;sub&gt;b&lt;/sub&gt; E[(1 + D(stop(x&lt;sub&gt;b&lt;/sub&gt;)))₊] + L&lt;sub&gt;R1&lt;/sub&gt;,    b ∈ {rand, style, rec}." vertex="1" parent="notes" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=0;fontFamily=Times New Roman;fontSize=22;fontStyle=0;fontColor=#202020;">
          <mxGeometry x="64" y="1414" width="2752" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="explain-3" value="L&lt;sub&gt;adv&lt;/sub&gt; = −(1/3) ∑&lt;sub&gt;b&lt;/sub&gt; E[D(x&lt;sub&gt;b&lt;/sub&gt;)];    L&lt;sub&gt;CTC&lt;/sub&gt; = λ&lt;sub&gt;r&lt;/sub&gt; CTC(R(x&lt;sub&gt;rand&lt;/sub&gt;), y′) + λ&lt;sub&gt;s&lt;/sub&gt; CTC(R(x&lt;sub&gt;style&lt;/sub&gt;), y′);    L&lt;sub&gt;writer&lt;/sub&gt; = CE(W(B(x&lt;sub&gt;style&lt;/sub&gt;)), w)." vertex="1" parent="notes" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=0;fontFamily=Times New Roman;fontSize=22;fontStyle=0;fontColor=#202020;">
          <mxGeometry x="64" y="1464" width="2752" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="explain-4" value="L&lt;sub&gt;G,E&lt;/sub&gt; = L&lt;sub&gt;adv&lt;/sub&gt; + 0.45 L&lt;sub&gt;adv,P&lt;/sub&gt; + L&lt;sub&gt;CTC&lt;/sub&gt; + 0.5 L&lt;sub&gt;writer&lt;/sub&gt; + λ&lt;sub&gt;rec&lt;/sub&gt; L&lt;sub&gt;rec&lt;/sub&gt; + L&lt;sub&gt;info&lt;/sub&gt; + L&lt;sub&gt;cycle&lt;/sub&gt; + 0.02 L&lt;sub&gt;content&lt;/sub&gt; + 0.1 L&lt;sub&gt;ctx&lt;/sub&gt; + 0.1 L&lt;sub&gt;KL&lt;/sub&gt;." vertex="1" parent="notes" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=0;fontFamily=Times New Roman;fontSize=22;fontStyle=0;fontColor=#202020;">
          <mxGeometry x="64" y="1514" width="2752" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="explain-5" value="D/P update every batch; G/E update every second critic batch. In the G/E phase, D/P/B/R/W parameters are frozen but input gradients remain. R and W+B are pretrained on real images; W+B starts from the OCR CNN. See (b)/(c) for the other losses." vertex="1" parent="notes" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=0;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=18;fontStyle=0;fontColor=#202020;">
          <mxGeometry x="64" y="1564" width="2752" height="37" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="explain-6" value="Normal config: λ_r 1→0.4 (epochs 10–20), λ_s 0.5→0.20 (8–28), λ_rec 10→2.5 (24–42). Lazy R1 = (0.01 × 32 / 2) E||∇_x D(x)||² every 32 critic batches. D includes the same mild differentiable augmentation policy for real and fake." vertex="1" parent="notes" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=0;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=18;fontStyle=0;fontColor=#202020;">
          <mxGeometry x="64" y="1611" width="2752" height="37" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="explain-7" value="Repeated target y′ and writer ID w boxes are the same ground-truth batch labels, not additional inputs to E or G. They are placed beside CTC/CE to keep supervision wires short." vertex="1" parent="notes" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=0;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=18;fontStyle=0;fontColor=#202020;">
          <mxGeometry x="64" y="1658" width="2752" height="37" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="source" value="ALPHA · 7eed74c6b2 · 2026-10-15 · Reference and random priors are distinct style sources; nested mini-diagrams share the same model parameters." vertex="1" parent="notes" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=0;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=13;fontStyle=0;fontColor=#202020;">
          <mxGeometry x="64" y="1920" width="2752" height="24" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
