        <mxCell id="title" value="(b) Regularization with reconstruction" vertex="1" parent="notes" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=0;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=30;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#202020;">
          <mxGeometry x="64" y="28" width="2752" height="48" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="subtitle" value="Image reconstruction and two global-code recovery paths share G/E; the local tokens are deterministic and have no KL term" vertex="1" parent="notes" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=0;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=17;fontStyle=0;fontColor=#202020;">
          <mxGeometry x="64" y="88" width="2752" height="32" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="legend" value="C1: global/local E   ·   C2: content-first fusion   ·   C3: StrokePatchD/crops   |   Solid: forward   ·   Dashed: loss/target   ·   Green: global-style conditioning" vertex="1" parent="notes" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=0;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=16;fontStyle=0;fontColor=#202020;">
          <mxGeometry x="64" y="1272" width="2752" height="28" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="explain-0" value="What is reconstructed — and what is not" vertex="1" parent="notes" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=0;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=21;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#202020;">
          <mxGeometry x="64" y="1320" width="2752" height="37" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="explain-1" value="Pixel L1 compares x_rec to the canonical real image x over valid pixels, not to the original-width style reference. Global information recovery reconstructs the prior z_g; transfer cycle recovers the reference global mean. These are separate targets, not three copies of one loss." vertex="1" parent="notes" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=0;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=18;fontStyle=0;fontColor=#202020;">
          <mxGeometry x="64" y="1367" width="2752" height="37" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="explain-2" value="L&lt;sub&gt;rec&lt;/sub&gt; = mean&lt;sub&gt;valid&lt;/sub&gt; |x&lt;sub&gt;rec&lt;/sub&gt; − x|;    L&lt;sub&gt;info&lt;/sub&gt; = mean |E&lt;sub&gt;g&lt;/sub&gt;(B(x&lt;sub&gt;rand&lt;/sub&gt;)) − stop(z&lt;sub&gt;g&lt;/sub&gt;)| / 8;    L&lt;sub&gt;cycle&lt;/sub&gt; = mean |E&lt;sub&gt;g&lt;/sub&gt;(B(x&lt;sub&gt;style&lt;/sub&gt;)) − stop(μ&lt;sub&gt;g,ref&lt;/sub&gt;)| / 8." vertex="1" parent="notes" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=0;fontFamily=Times New Roman;fontSize=22;fontStyle=0;fontColor=#202020;">
          <mxGeometry x="64" y="1414" width="2752" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="explain-3" value="L&lt;sub&gt;KL&lt;/sub&gt; = KL[N(μ&lt;sub&gt;g&lt;/sub&gt;, diag(exp(ℓ&lt;sub&gt;g&lt;/sub&gt;))) || N(0,I)] / 8;    g = μ&lt;sub&gt;g&lt;/sub&gt; + exp(0.5 ℓ&lt;sub&gt;g&lt;/sub&gt;) ⊙ ε;    ε ∼ N(0,I);    ℓ&lt;sub&gt;g&lt;/sub&gt; = log σ&lt;sub&gt;g&lt;/sub&gt;²." vertex="1" parent="notes" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=0;fontFamily=Times New Roman;fontSize=22;fontStyle=0;fontColor=#202020;">
          <mxGeometry x="64" y="1464" width="2752" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="explain-4" value="L&lt;sub&gt;content&lt;/sub&gt; = balanced-BCE(Probe(GRL(μ&lt;sub&gt;g,ref&lt;/sub&gt;)), bag(y)) / 8;    GRL is identity forward and reverses only the gradient toward E." vertex="1" parent="notes" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=0;fontFamily=Times New Roman;fontSize=22;fontStyle=0;fontColor=#202020;">
          <mxGeometry x="64" y="1514" width="2752" height="40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="explain-5" value="The probe learns reference character presence while E is pushed to hide it in g. Local L is a deterministic, centered 7-token residual; it is neither KL-regularized nor reconstructed against random local slots. E_g skips local retrieval. All repeated B/E/G blocks share weights." vertex="1" parent="notes" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=0;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=18;fontStyle=0;fontColor=#202020;">
          <mxGeometry x="64" y="1564" width="2752" height="37" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="explain-6" value="These three generated branches also receive the global and patch adversarial losses in (a)/(c). Only x_rand and x_style receive OCR CTC. The /8 factors preserve the explicit eight-token normalization implemented in the current loss functions." vertex="1" parent="notes" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=0;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=18;fontStyle=0;fontColor=#202020;">
          <mxGeometry x="64" y="1611" width="2752" height="37" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="explain-7" value="The nearby μ_g target is a copy of E’s reference posterior mean, not a new encoder or trainable module. Repeating this target avoids a wire crossing the image-generation paths." vertex="1" parent="notes" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=0;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=18;fontStyle=0;fontColor=#202020;">
          <mxGeometry x="64" y="1658" width="2752" height="37" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="source" value="ALPHA · 7eed74c6b2 · 2026-10-15 · Reference and random priors are distinct style sources; nested mini-diagrams share the same model parameters." vertex="1" parent="notes" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=0;fontFamily=Arial;fontSize=13;fontStyle=0;fontColor=#202020;">
          <mxGeometry x="64" y="1920" width="2752" height="24" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
